From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GRENET <mathieu@mgth.fr>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:59:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] demux/dovi_split: carry the BL packet position to the
 EL packet

The EL packet mirrored the BL packet's pts, dts, duration and keyframe
flag, but not its file position. In Matroska the HEVC packets carry no
DTS, so the EL queue was left with neither a monotonic DTS nor a
monotonic position, and initiate_refresh_seek() refused the refresh seek
for every track switch while the EL stream was selected ("can't issue
refresh seek").

Without the refresh seek, the newly selected audio track starts at the
demuxer's read-ahead position. With the cache enabled (any network
mount), that is up to demuxer-max-bytes ahead: on a ~60 Mb/s Dolby Vision
FEL remux, audio stayed silent for 18-20 s after the switch, waiting for
video to catch up.

Copy the position as well. A track switch now issues the refresh seek
and audio resumes within ~0.3 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 demux/dovi_split.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/demux/dovi_split.c b/demux/dovi_split.c
index cfe27185da..c9a435ab7b 100644
--- a/demux/dovi_split.c
+++ b/demux/dovi_split.c
@@ -192,8 +192,12 @@ struct demux_packet *mp_dovi_split_dispatch(struct mp_dovi_split *s,
         new_demux_packet_from_avpacket(s->demuxer->packet_pool, s->staging);
     if (dp) {
         // Mirror the BL packet's timing so the pairing filter can match by PTS.
+        // The file position too: without it (and with no DTS, as in mkv HEVC)
+        // the EL queue has no monotonic key, and the demuxer refuses the
+        // refresh seek a track switch needs.
         dp->pts = bl_dp->pts;
         dp->dts = bl_dp->dts;
+        dp->pos = bl_dp->pos;
         dp->duration = bl_dp->duration;
         dp->keyframe = bl_dp->keyframe;
         dp->stream = s->el->index;
